Description: Mark the access keys of the menus which Firefox exports over D-Bus as their mnemonics.
 With the global menu bar (widget.gtk.global-menu.enabled), Firefox exports the menus of its menu bar with the
 dbusmenu protocol, whose labels mark the mnemonic with an underscore before its letter, as GTK labels do. Firefox
 exported the plain labels, so the desktop could neither underline the access keys nor open a menu with Alt and its
 letter, and an underscore in a label, as in a page title in the History menu, marked a mnemonic the item does not
 have and was not shown. The labels now mark the access key where the menus in the window underline it
 (MozTextLabel.formatAccessKey in toolkit/content/widgets/text.js): at its first occurrence in the label, or else
 appended in parentheses, as some locales always do. Underscores in the labels are doubled.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: no
